{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204476-nodes-of-legend","id":1204476,"title":"Nodes of legend","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-08T02:14:44-07:00","id":1204476,"title":"Nodes of legend","content":"I have been reading the Book of Chantries, and it has a lot to say about nodes. First, being at old as it is, the scale of Quintessence is off completely compared to M20, with basics nodes offering 10 points of Quintessence a day, which would be a 12 to 70 points Node in M20.<br /> <br /> One of the most interesting fact, however, is that Stonehenge, powering Doissetep, is described as the 3rd most powerful node in the world.<br /> Was there ever another mention of a node ranking? What node could, in your opinion, be more powerful than Stonehenge?<br /> <br /> Some of the best options are ancient monuments and religious sites, both of which can describe Stonehenge. The Pyramids are as ancient as they get, and are linked to the Underworld. However, it's likely that Mages wouldn't control them, as the characters of Mummy would take offence to it (I don't have enough experience with that gane line to say).<br /> <br /> Big temples like Angkor Wat, the Vatican or Mecca are also a possibility, having almost as much gravitas as Stonehenge, plus the weight of millions of faithful believers. However, they are too urban, too popular for what Nodes are, being places that people are, rather than look at.<br /> <br /> We could look at modern monuments, rife with symbolism. Things like the Statue of Liberty have as much value and respect as religions, in a way (look at the modern gods in Scion like Uncle Sam). Being recent is the main drawback of these as ultra-powerful nodes, but is not a hard stop, Dachau being given as an exemple of node fueling the Realm of Voormas.<br /> <br /> Finally, all of these examples are somewhat Tradition oriented. It's hard to imagine that in the 3 most powerful nodes in the world, none belong to the Technocracy. So, we have to look at the biggest locations of technocratic values. Wall street is probably the biggest Primal Venture there, but is it at the level of Stonehenge in Quintessence generation? As for science, do we look to labs (CERN is pushing the limits of the Consensus), accomplishements (the ISS is the biggest scientific endeavor humanity has tackled), or areas where technocratic paradigm is strongest (schools where it's taught maybe)?<br /> <br /> What are your ideas for the 1st and 2nd strongest nodes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24094-banirien","name":"baniRien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T06:10:00-07:00","id":1299931,"title":"","content":"Atlantis.<br /> Machu Picchu.<br /> Cleopatra's tomb.<br /> Dwarka.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T14:13:28-07:00","id":1300087,"title":"","content":"I think the Great Pyramids of Egypt, as the only surviving ancient Wonder of the World, should qualify. I don't think nodes necessarily have to be in mages' hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T17:31:22-07:00","id":1300150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baniRien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1204476-nodes-of-legend#post1204476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the most interesting fact, however, is that Stonehenge, powering Doissetep, is described as the 3rd most powerful node in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still wonder just how absolutely pissed the Gardeners Of The Tree must be for the Hermetics having gotten their hands on that one...or were, either way. Could be an amusing story hook for another aspect to Doissetep's downfall...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T22:17:24-07:00","id":1301230,"title":"","content":"Victoria Falls/&quot;The Smoke that Thunders&quot; in Zimbabwe/Zambia<br /> Mount Wingen/Burning Mountain in New South Wales<br /> The Oklo region uranium deposits in Gabon prior to their being mined<br /> Mounts Fuji, Tate, and Haku in Japan<br /> The Grand Canyon prior to the building of the Glen Canyon Dam<br /> The tomb of the first Qin Emperor in China<br /> The Great Serpent Mound in Ohio <br /> Tikal/Yax Mutal in Guatemala <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T13:29:13-07:00","id":1301389,"title":"","content":"Ayers Rock, AKA Uluru(spelling?) In Australia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T21:49:07-07:00","id":1301506,"title":"","content":"I feel like the winner would need to be something very strong consistent emotion from a large quantity of people, based on that:<br /> Kaaba in Mecca as #1 <br /> St. Peter's Basilica as #2<br /> The Padmanabhaswamy Temple as an alternate to one of the above.<br /> <br /> Maybe due to age, Mt. Fuji or Bialowieza Forest.<br /> <br /> I wonder if there are places that are potent but inaccessible like for instance the epicenter of an earthquake or the heart of a hurricane.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:54:02-07:00","id":1302003,"title":"","content":"Everest seems likely to be an untapped node. Definitely agree on the pyramids too.<br /> <br /> As for the difference in power between 1e and m20 nodes and chantries, I recall reading something (I think in the 2nd ed Storyteller handbook Book of Mirrors) about how in 1E the idea was that nodes were rare; there was s sort of oil war happening over them because quintessence only came from those and avatars. But, then the idea of quintessence permeating reality came around and though nodes are still useful they aren't as necessary. My guess is that they decided to increase the availability of power from a given node to reflect both the demand needed for quintessence in Doisstep and make them more impressive as a background option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T17:13:32-07:00","id":1302059,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Everest is the tallest, but isn't Mount Kailash the one that's sacred to several major religions?<br /> <br /> Though I guess if you count all those dead mountaineers littered all over Everest as sacrifices from pilgrimages, it could have built up quite a charge too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:30:55-07:00","id":1302092,"title":"","content":"Some powerful nodes are likely to be hidden, or at least completely unknown to the mundane world. Lost caves, hidden glens, ancient trees and the like. A lot of James Rollins's early books (before he switched over to just doing his Sigma Force series) had a lot of fascinating areas with weird and uncanny goings on. Amazonia, Excavation, Subterranean, Ice Hunt, Sandstorm, and Deep Fathom were his early ones. There's also places like the ancient burial ground in Pet Semitary, or the Nexis of All Realities from Marvel's old Man-Thing comics. <br /> <br /> There's also the possibility of more modern man-made constructs that channel Quintessence, similar to Ivo Shandor's building in Ghostbusters, or modern high energy particle accelerators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}